# espRotary board identification — 2026-09-11

## What appeared on USB
  node          /dev/cu.usbmodem21101   (also /dev/tty.usbmodem21101)
  vendor        Espressif, VID 0x303a
  USB mode      USB-Serial/JTAG — native, no bridge chip
  chip          ESP32-S3 (QFN56) revision v0.2
  features      Wi-Fi, BT 5 (LE), dual core + LP core, 240 MHz, 8 MB embedded PSRAM
  crystal       40 MHz
  MAC           68:ee:8f:5d:b3:74
  flash         JEDEC ba 4018 — 16 MB, quad I/O, 3.3 V

## Not the reTerminal
  reTerminal E1002   CH340 bridge 1a86:7523, /dev/cu.usbserial-*, MAC e0:72:a1:f9:02:60
  espRotary          native 303a,           /dev/cu.usbmodem*,     MAC 68:ee:8f:5d:b3:74
  Same silicon and revision, different boards — the MAC settles it.

## Baud
  --baud 921600   read died after 20 kB: 'Serial data stream stopped'
  default         256 kB in 1.4 s at 1460 kbit/s; 16 MB in 96.9 s at 1384 kbit/s
  USB CDC has no UART to reclock, so the baud argument is meaningless here.
